  "requirement": "Distinguishes a domain operation failure, a missing agent, a provider connection or request failure, an agent protocol failure, and an error encoding or decoding the output.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub enum ValidationError<E> {\n    Graph(E),\n    NoAgentConfigured,\n    Agent(String),\n    Provider(std::io::Error),\n    Output(serde_json::Error),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<E: Debug> Debug for ValidationError<E>;\nimpl<E: Display> Display for ValidationError<E>;\nimpl<E: Error + 'static> Error for ValidationError<E>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The text prescribes a public generic enum `ValidationError<E>` with five variants (`Graph(E)`, `NoAgentConfigured`, `Agent(String)`, `Provider(std::io::Error)`, `Output(serde_json::Error)`). It also prescribes three trait implementations with specific bounds. Changing any of these would change the declared type or its trait surface, so they are structural obligations. The roots cover all of them.\n\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#enum[ValidationError]` declares exactly those variants and payload types. `#[derive(Debug)]` gives `impl<E: Debug> Debug`, which satisfies the `Debug` requirement.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#impl[ValidationError<E>/std::fmt::Display]` is `impl<E: std::fmt::Display> Display`, matching the prescribed bound.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#impl[ValidationError<E>/std::error::Error]` is `impl<E: std::error::Error + 'static> Error`, matching the prescribed bound. It has a `source` method.\n\nAll three roots carry `{impl}` markers. No other root is needed.\n\nbehavioral: `requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.ValidationError` states one behavioral obligation. The error type must distinguish five failure kinds, and it must be usable through `Debug`, `Display` and `Error`. The reviewed tests cover each kind, and none of them contradicts the requirement.\n\n- **`Graph(E)`**: `tests/contracts.rs#fn[refresh_propagates_load_decode_check_execution_and_save_errors]` runs the load, read, edges, execute and store stages. For each stage it asserts that the domain error comes back as `ValidationError::Graph` with the same payload. It also asserts that the saved record is unchanged. `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload]` checks that `Graph.source()` returns the inner error.\n- **`NoAgentConfigured`**: `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` asserts that `verify` without an agent returns this variant. It also asserts that nothing is read or stored.\n- **`Agent(String)`**:\n  - `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[ending_without_a_corrected_submission_is_an_agent_error]` and `agent/tests.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` assert that a protocol failure gives `Agent`. The second test is the case where the model returns only text.\n  - `agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload` asserts that the payload is a `String`, that `Display` gives `agent: provider detail`, and that `source()` is `None`.\n- **`Provider(std::io::Error)`**: `agent/tests.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` asserts `Provider` with a message containing the provider failure text. `agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors]` asserts `Provider` and a `Display` string naming the missing credential variable.\n- **`Output(serde_json::Error)`**: `tests/contracts.rs#fn[refresh_serialization_failure_preserves_the_saved_record]` and `tests/contracts.rs#fn[serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged]` assert `Output` for encoding failures. The refresh test for decode failures asserts `Output` for the decode, stale decode and unversioned decode stages.\n- **Trait implementations**: `Display` is asserted for `Agent` and `Provider`, and `Error::source` for `Graph` and `Agent`. `Debug` is exercised in the failure message of the refresh test.\n\nThe requirement does not fix `Display` wording or `source` behavior for the other variants, so those need no further tests. I found no unacknowledged gap.",
